<title>LITHUANIA: SNAIGE SAYS TALKING TO WESTERN INVESTOR.</title>
<headline>SNAIGE SAYS TALKING TO WESTERN INVESTOR.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refrigerator maker Snaige on Tuesday said the investor with which it was talking on the possible sale of a stake was from the West.</p>
<p>Company director general Antanas Andriulionis earlier told Reuters that the company was plannng to boost its share capital to 60 million litas from 20 million litas and that it was in talks with a possible strategic investor.</p>
<p>He later confirmed that the investor was a Western company but refused to give any more details.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 223 517</p>
